From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:03:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] softisp: apply frame timing and refresh configured sensor information

Preserve frame-duration requests when moving from the old simple IPA to
upstream's shared AGC. Rebase the timing correction from the previous
ThinkSmart queue onto the new SoftISP configuration and session
structures.

Forward VBLANK and apply it before exposure. Restore native blanking on
same-mode reopen, refresh the sensor's control range, and configure the
IPA with current mode geometry and pixel timing rather than
initialization-time values.

Reserve the sensor's exposure margin, round frame length upwards and
clamp it to physical VBLANK bounds. Report duration from the controls
applied to the captured frame rather than echoing a request.

Report exposure and analogue gain from those same captured-frame sensor
controls, not from the AGC state prepared for another frame. Delayed
sensor controls and changing frame-rate requests must not produce
results that pair a planned exposure with an already-applied frame
duration.

Finalize the exposure/gain/VBLANK command together after processing
statistics. Upstream prepares exposure from the previous automatic state
but computes VBLANK from the new state; statistics are intentionally
skipped on three out of four frames, and the generic no-statistics path
otherwise resets VBLANK to the minimum. Neither path may combine a
retained long exposure with a short frame. Use an opt-in shared AGC
sensor-control preparation helper to retain coherent timing on skipped
frames and to honor a lowered FPS-range maximum without reprocessing
stale statistics. Other hardware IPA preparation paths remain unchanged.

Exercise native-duration truncation, requested-frame-rate quantization,
the physical frame-length maximum, skipped statistics and a reduced
frame-duration budget in AGC regression tests. Do not carry over
empirical stretchGain or maximum-frame-time tuning caps.

Base-commit: df8e348d64b4932a0676256ed24f0da3ee9438bc
Source: https://github.com/alessandro-fontana/android_external_libcamera/commit/20d7d37a4d7c88721f5604a5da4c9e461434ef38
---
